Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:08:03 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 26/38] dt-bindings: leds: backlight: Add Exynos9810 DSIM DCS
 backlight

Panels such as the Himax HX83102E in the Galaxy Tab Active3 drive the
LED PWM themselves and take their brightness as DCS 0x51 over DSI.
Until there is a DECON/DSIM DRM driver for Exynos9810, the display keeps
running as the bootloader set it up and brightness can only be changed
by queueing DCS packets into the command FIFOs of the running DSIM
links. Describe that device: one or two DSIM register windows (dual
DSI) and the usual backlight properties.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../samsung,exynos9810-dsim-backlight.yaml    | 59 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 59 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/samsung,exynos9810-dsim-backlight.yaml

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/samsung,exynos9810-dsim-backlight.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/samsung,exynos9810-dsim-backlight.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..2bf4309e3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/backlight/samsung,exynos9810-dsim-backlight.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,59 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/leds/backlight/samsung,exynos9810-dsim-backlight.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: DCS backlight on a bootloader-initialised Exynos9810 DSIM
+
+maintainers:
+  - dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
+
+description: |
+  Some MIPI DSI panels, such as the Himax HX83102E in the Samsung Galaxy Tab
+  Active3, generate their LED PWM themselves and take the brightness over
+  DSI (DCS SET_DISPLAY_BRIGHTNESS, 0x51). While the Exynos9810 DECON and
+  DSIM are still running as set up by the bootloader and the kernel only
+  uses its framebuffer, brightness is set by queueing DCS packets into the
+  command FIFOs of the DSIM links. Nothing else of the display pipeline is
+  touched. The same packet is sent on every link, so a dual-DSI panel lists
+  both.
+
+allOf:
+  - $ref: common.yaml#
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: samsung,exynos9810-dsim-backlight
+
+  reg:
+    minItems: 1
+    items:
+      - description: registers of the first DSIM link
+      - description: registers of the second DSIM link (dual DSI)
+
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 2
+
+  default-brightness: true
+
+  max-brightness:
+    description:
+      Highest DCS brightness value. Values above 255 are sent as two
+      bytes, most significant byte first.
+    maximum: 65535
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+
+additionalProperties: false
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    backlight@16080000 {
+        compatible = "samsung,exynos9810-dsim-backlight";
+        reg = <0x16080000 0x100>, <0x16090000 0x100>;
+        max-brightness = <3977>;
+        default-brightness = <928>;
+    };
